esponsible for conducting market clearing based on security constraints during centralized bidding, and verifying the final trading outcomes in coordination with the power dispatching institution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"An entity responsible for performing safety verification on trading results after market clearing to ensure grid stability and operational reliability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家发展改革委\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A national government authority responsible for reviewing and approving transmission loss levels and related policies for cross-provincial and inter-regional transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A national government agency involved in overseeing energy policy and regulation, including the approval of transmission loss standards and implementation of cross-provincial and inter-regional transaction rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"优先发电政策\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A policy framework ensuring certain power generation units, such as combined heat and power plants and waste-heat recovery units, receive guaranteed generation rights. These specific electricity quantities cannot be transferred.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可再生能源调峰机组\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A category of power generation units designed to support renewable energy integration by providing flexibility in the grid. Their priority generation electricity can be transferred.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"合同转让交易\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A transaction mechanism allowing market participants who hold contracts such as direct trading or cross-provincial and inter-regional contracts to transfer their contract volumes. The transferee must meet market access conditions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"输电损耗\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The electrical energy lost during transmission across long-distance power lines. It is either included in the transmission price or calculated separately and typically borne by the buyer unless otherwise agreed.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"受电落地价格\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"The total cost of electricity received at the destination region, composed of the transaction price (sending price), transmission cost (fee), and transmission losses.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"购销差价不变\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A pricing mechanism used in regions without separate transmission pricing, where the difference between purchase and sale prices remains constant, despite changes in wholesale prices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"峰谷电价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A pricing model where electricity rates vary by time of day—peak, flat, and valley periods—commonly applied to certain users who can continue using it even when participating in direct trading.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"辅助服务考核与补偿机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A system that allows electricity users to share the costs of grid balancing services, such as frequency regulation and load following, either through performance-based penalties or compensation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"现货市场\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A future electricity market phase that has not yet been launched, where real-time or short-term electricity trading will occur. Prior to its launch, grid companies may represent non-market participants in cross-provincial and inter-regional transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"年度交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A periodic electricity trading event conducted annually, following a defined sequence including the determination of internal priority generation and execution of contractual obligations.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"双边协商交易\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"Market entities engage in bilateral negotiation to determine electricity volume and price, forming initial trading intentions before formal confirmation.\"|>\"market participation, negotiation process\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"集中竞价交易\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"The power trading institution conducts market clearing based on security constraints, playing a central role in determining the outcome of centralized bidding.\"|>\"market clearing, institutional role\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"集中竞价交易\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The p