    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"预挂牌月平衡偏差方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Pre-announcement monthly balance deviation method refers to a mechanism where the dispatching authority determines the priority ranking of upward and downward regulated units for the next month through pre-announcement, based on increasing generation price (from low to high) and compensation price (from low to high), respectively. It is used to manage electricity supply-demand balance under grid safety constraints.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"等比例调整方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Equal proportion adjustment method involves daily tracking of each power generation enterprise's contract execution rate after monthly trading, aiming to maintain similar total contract execution rates across similar units, with next-day generation plans adjusted accordingly. Excess or deficient generation is allocated proportionally based on monthly plan and market contract volumes, settled at weighted average contract prices.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"滚动调整方式\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Rolling adjustment method applies in regions with low release ratio of power generation plans. Priority generation and base electricity quantities are adjusted monthly on a rolling basis, while user-side contract electricity can be settled monthly or rolled over. Imbalances in contracts due to this method may be addressed through post-event electricity contract transfer transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Auxiliary services refer to grid support services including basic and paid services, such as peak regulation, automatic generation control, reserve capacity, reactive power, and black start. These services are provided by power plants, users, independent providers, and third parties, with compensation based on service effectiveness.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power dispatching authority is responsible for monitoring system operation, determining auxiliary service needs, managing generation schedules, and ensuring grid safety and balance during real-time operations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises are entities that produce electricity and participate in market transactions. They are subject to contract execution tracking, performance evaluation, and financial adjustments based on over-generation or under-generation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users are market participants who consume electricity and may provide auxiliary services, especially in demand response. They are liable for deviation charges and may receive compensation if they contribute positively to grid balancing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"储能设备\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Energy storage devices are encouraged to participate in providing auxiliary services, contributing to grid stability and flexibility.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"第三方\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Third-party providers are allowed to offer auxiliary services, expanding the pool of available resources for grid support.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"跨省跨区交易送端地区发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises in sending regions of inter-provincial and inter-regional transactions are included in the auxiliary service management scope of receiving regions and may receive or pay compensation based on the services they provide.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"受端电网\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The receiving power grid is the regional grid that receives electricity from other regions via inter-provincial or inter-regional transmission lines and has specific requirements for ancillary services like peak regulation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"主电能表\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The main energy meter is installed at the metering point and serves as the primary data source for electricity settlement, with its readings being legally binding for billing purposes.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"副电能表\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The secondary energy meter is installed alongside the main meter for reference purposes; it replaces the main meter’s data only when the main meter is confirmed faulty.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"负荷控制系统\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Load control systems are infrastructure components used to monitor and manage electricity consumption, supporting demand-side management and response.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"用电信息采集系统\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity information collection systems gather real-time data on power usage, enabling monitoring, analysis, and implementation of demand-side responses.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"需求侧响应\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Demand-side response refers to actions taken by consumers to adjust their electricity usage in response to grid signals, helping to balance supply and demand, especially during peak periods.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电能服务\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electric energy services are value-added offerings that help users manage energy use efficiently and participate in electricity markets.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Market trading refers to the process of buying and selling electricity through monthly or real-time mechanisms, governed by established rules and procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电量结算\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Electricity settlement is the process of finalizing billing based on actual metering data, including corrections due to meter faults or discrepancies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"偏差考核费用\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Deviation assessment fees are financial penalties imposed on users or generators for deviations from planned electricity usage or generation, which are then partially returned to generators based on their share of electricity or revenue.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"事后合同电量转让交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Post-event contract electricity transfer transactions allow market participants to correct imbalances in contract execution resulting from adjustment methods like equal proportion or rolling adjustments.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"调峰补偿费用\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Peak regulation compensation fees are payments made to participants who provide load-shifting or regulating services to balance grid peaks, with some exemptions granted to users contributing positively to system balance.\")##\n\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"预挂牌月平衡偏差方式\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching authority uses the pre-announcement monthly balance deviation method to determine the order of unit activation for balancing supply and demand, ensuring grid safety.\"|>\"grid scheduling, balancing mechanism\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"等比例调整方式\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching authority implements the equal proportion adjustment method by monitoring contract execution rates daily and adjusting next-day generation plans accordingly.\"|>\"operational management, contract tracking\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"滚动调整方式\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching authority applies the rolling adjustment method in low-release regions, managing monthly adjustments of priority generation and base electricity quantities.\"|>\"planning flexibility, contract management\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching authority determines the need for auxiliary services and manages their provision, including setting demand levels and selecting providers through competitive bidding.\"|>\"service coordination, grid stability\"|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises provide auxiliary services and are compensated based on the effectiveness of their contribution, following uniform standards.\"|>\"service provision, compensation\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"Electricity users can provide auxiliary services, particularly through demand response, and are compensated uniformly with generators.\"|>\"demand-side participation, compensation\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"储能设备\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"Energy storage devices are encouraged to participate in providing auxiliary services, enhancing grid flexibility and reliability.\"|>\"energy storage, grid support\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"第三方\"<|>\"辅助服务\"<|>\"Third-party providers are allowed to deliver auxiliary services, increasing competition and resource availability.\"|>\"market expansion, service diversity\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"跨省跨区交易送端地区发电企业\"<|>\"受端电网\"<|>\"Sending-region power generators are subject to the auxiliary service management rules of the receiving region and must meet its requirements for peak regulation and other services.\"|>\"inter-regional compliance, service integration\"|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"主电能表\"<|>\"副电能表\"<|>\"The main and secondary energy meters are installed together at the same metering point, with the secondary serving as backup and replacing the main meter only upon confirmation of fault.\"|>\"meter redundancy, data integrity\"|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"负荷控制系统\"<|>\"用电信息采集系统\"<|>\"Both systems are foundational technologies used in demand-side management, working together to monitor and control electricity consumption in real time.\"|>\"infrastructure integration, data collection\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"需求侧响应\"<|>\"电能服务\"<|>\"Demand-side response is facilitated by electric energy services that help users optimize their consumption patterns and participate in market mechanisms.\"|>\"energy optimization, market participation\"|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"偏差考核费用\"<|>\"事后合同电量转让交易\"<|>\"When imbalance occurs due to deviation, the associated fees lead to the possibility of post-event contract transfers to rebalance obligations.\"|>\"financial correction, market adjustment\"|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电量结算\"<|>\"主电能表\"<|>\"The main energy meter's data is the official basis for electricity settlement, forming the foundation of billing accuracy.\"|>\"billing accuracy, measurement standard\"|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"调峰补偿费用\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"Electricity users may be exempted from paying peak regulation compensation fees if they demonstrate positive contributions to grid balancing through their load profiles.\"|>\"incentive mechanism, cost reduction\"|>8)##\n\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"electricity market mechanisms, auxiliary services, grid balancing, demand-side management, contract execution, metering and settlement, inter-regional transmission, deviation management, competitive bidding, energy storage\")<|COMPLETE|>"
